rovides various software, such as Mosaic One SaaS, n-Command, Procloud, MCP, AOE, and ACI-E. It serves large, medium, and small service providers; alternative service providers, such as utilities, municipalities and fiber overbuilders; cable/MSOs; and SMBs and distributed enterprises. ADTRAN Holdings, Inc. was incorporated in 1985 and is headquartered in Huntsville, Alabama.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas Richard Stanton | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 60 | Compensation: $3.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $339K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers. Each employee generates $31K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 12\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["ADTRAN Holdings, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $394M market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at -29% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 44%.","The business throws off $98M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -0.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.7% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_he